goto_definition — implementation plan
======================================

status: planned (2026-07-09)

wave 4, navigation: POSITION-based lookup (the ctrl-click mirror),
pure scala over the PIDE snapshot — no ML, no bridge. complements
plans/find_definition; requires the theory to be use_theories-loaded
(snapshots only exist for checked documents).

advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          goto_definition
description   "Jump from a USE of a name to its definition, given a
              position in a loaded theory: pass the theory's long
              name plus `offset` (character offset) or `pattern` (a
              literal source substring; its first occurrence marks
              the spot). Works on anything under the cursor —
              constants, facts, type constructors inside annotations,
              ML antiquotations — using the checked document's entity
              markup, with no name guessing. Reports the entity's
              kind and its definition site (file, line, offset).
              Only theories loaded with load_theory have the needed
              markup; for image theories use find_definition
              instead."
inputSchema   {"type": "object",
               "properties": {
                 "theory": {"type": "string"},
                 "offset": {"type": "integer"},
                 "pattern": {"type": "string"}},
               "required": ["theory"]}
              (exactly one of offset/pattern; handler-enforced.)
annotations   {"readOnlyHint": true, "idempotentHint": true,
               "openWorldHint": false}
outputSchema  none.

name/argument mapping across the layers
---------------------------------------

  mcp client edge   tools/call "goto_definition",
                    {"theory": "Draft.Nav_Test", "pattern": "rev xs"}
  scala builtin row resolve the snapshot for the node (shared
                    snapshot access from plans/repl_init_from_source
                    step 1); locate the range (offset directly, or
                    pattern -> first occurrence range); snapshot
                    cumulate over Rendering.entity_elements at that
                    range; extract Position.Def_File / Def_Line /
                    Def_Offset + Markup.kind from the entity
                    properties; format hits. no engine.

implementation steps
--------------------

1. [infra shared] the snapshot/command access on MCP_Session (same
